+# RTLink/Plus overlay analysis and DOS launch support
+
+## Scope
+
+`fdisbull.rtlink` implements a bounded reader for the embedded RTLink/Plus v2
+layout observed in the supplied Dragonsphere SPHERE.EXE. It provides the
+projectless CLI/JSON methods `rtlink-inspect`, `rtlink-extract` and
+`rtlink-disasm`, and a Python API. It neither executes inputs nor invokes an
+external RTLink tool. It is not a universal RTLink decoder.
+
+The detailed agent guide is
+[src/fdisbull/skills/fdisbull-investigate/references/dos-formats.md](../src/fdisbull/skills/fdisbull-investigate/references/dos-formats.md).
+It separates COM/MZ headers, modern executable stubs, CPU modes, overlays,
+packers, game-resource formats, guest interpreters and launch requirements.
+
+## Data contract
+
+The resident MZ image is validated independently. A zero-offset resident
+relocation identifies a candidate segment; its index starts 48 bytes into
+that segment. This profile uses 32-byte rows, sequential IDs beginning at 2,
+a DWORD block file offset at row+8 and an ID at row+14. A zero ID terminates
+the sequence. Unsupported or ambiguous index candidates refuse.
+
+The embedded block's first words supply total paragraphs, header paragraphs,
+an opaque word, relocation start and relocation count. This implementation
+admits relocation start zero, with offset/segment pairs beginning at block+16.
+It validates header capacity, file extents, disk overlap and every relocated
+word against **available** payload bytes. Unknown index/header semantics are
+not used to infer gameplay behavior or executable entrypoints.
+
+Files ending inside a final declared paragraph can expose fewer payload bytes
+than the paragraph allocation. Up to 15 such terminal bytes are reported as
+unavailable, not supplied as zeros and not declared valid instructions. Larger
+truncations or relocations into the absent span refuse. Other overlays must
+have their complete declared span. This reporting is not proof that an
+unavailable byte is harmless padding.
+
+Each overlay has a stable source hash, ID, index offset, physical block/code
+range, payload hash, relocation records and unresolved entrypoint/code-data
+status. Repeated load-segment fields are retained, not merged. Static source
+coordinates do not establish runtime selectors, relocation bases or generations.
+
+## Operations
+
+```sh
+fdisbull rtlink-inspect /private/SPHERE.EXE
+fdisbull rtlink-disasm /private/SPHERE.EXE --overlay-id 2 --max-instructions 32
+fdisbull rtlink-extract /private/SPHERE.EXE /private/new-regions \
+  --expected-sha256 <exact-source-sha256>
+```
+
+Extraction writes the original resident load image and each available overlay
+payload separately, with a JSON manifest. No relocation is applied, no thunk
+is patched, and no new executable is emitted. Existing destinations and source
+symlinks refuse. Files are private original-derived payloads and must stay out
+of public Git, reports and tool packages. The original remains unchanged.
+
+Disassembly uses the existing iced-x86 16-bit decoder on a caller-selected
+region, under byte/instruction budgets. It stops on invalid decode or budget.
+The offset is **overlay-relative**, not a DOS address. Linear candidate decoding
+does not establish reachability or distinguish embedded data from instructions.
+The commands are discoverable through `methods`, and the capability catalog
+labels the feature partial/experimental. They are not a new CPU module or a
+replacement for the existing x86 processor.
+
+## Launch fixes
+
+The DOS debugger no longer discards explicit argument tokens. CLI `--arguments`
+accepts a JSON list, and `debug-launch` accepts the same `arguments` field. The
+narrow initial profile refuses whitespace, quotation and shell operators in
+tokens, enforces a DOS-tail budget, and rejects these options on other backends.
+
+`--cd-image` / `cd_image` admits one validated Mode-1 track from CUE/INS or a
+cooked ISO. The process gets an owned descriptor and a single authored
+`imgmount d ... -t iso` command. It does not read target-provided autoexec
+commands or ambient DOSBox configuration. CD source hashes/identities are
+recorded and checked before launch. C remains the selected game directory.
+This uses the existing native backend without patching its executable.
+
+The CUE parser accepts one- or two-digit TRACK and INDEX values, normalizes
+INDEX values before duplicate checks, and retains its path/traversal/mode
+restrictions. `disc-inspect` treats `.INS` as a descriptor candidate, which must
+pass the same content validation as `.cue`. Unrelated INS input is rejected.
+
+This is not generic arbitrary-drive mounting, a batch interpreter or an audio
+CD player. CD-mounted native checkpoint/rewind serialization is not qualified
+and is refused. In-game save/load and direct execution controls are separate.
+
+## Verification and provenance
+
+Synthetic tests build authored MZ and overlay containers, exercise rejection
+paths, compare exported bytes and verify bounded disassembly. Authored ISO
+fixtures and optional real DOSBox tests inspect the PSP argument tail, read
+`TEST` from D:\ONE.BIN, and verify child cleanup. Game-backed observations are
+separate and use private supplied files; no game bytes enter tests or this repo.
+
+Reference consulted: dreammaster/tools `rtlink_decode/variation2.cpp`, branch
+`rtlink_decode`, Git blob `d6dfccff3c143d04fc169bdf2606b99105413b34`:
+https://github.com/dreammaster/tools/blob/rtlink_decode/rtlink_decode/variation2.cpp
+The upstream source is GPL-2.0-or-later. No upstream C++ source or binaries are
+bundled. This Python implementation is newly authored, but its format layout
+and discovery rule were informed by that implementation. Review attribution
+and any derivative-work obligations with the project's licensing decision
+before public release; this document is not licensing clearance.
+
+The complete upstream tool also recognizes other layouts and creates a patched
+flat disassembly view. This module deliberately does not offer those unqualified
+paths. Future work: additional variant readers, independent loader witnesses,
+live overlay-generation mapping and resolved cross-overlay transfer evidence.
